name mig29-bfm-1
timeout 300                                  # sim-seconds until TIMEOUT

# THE MiG-29 BFM MEASURING RIG — the counterpart to bfm-basic, one airframe over. It exists to prove
# what doc/duels.md D1 and modules/mig29/module.md gap 4h left open: that this jet's close-combat
# control law is SURVIVABLE, and that from a trail position the MiG acquires, locks and leads a target
# on its own sensor — the same claim bfm-basic makes for the F-16, measured the same way.
#
# WHY A TRAIL SETUP AND A STRAIGHT DEFENDER, not the nose-on merge of duel-merge. duel-merge is the
# REPRODUCER (exit 2, a known departure); it stays as it is. This rig isolates the CONTROL LAW from the
# ACQUISITION problem: a straight-flying, co-speed defender 2 nm ahead is the geometry the N019's RAD
# pattern (+-30 deg az, +-6 deg el) can actually hold, so the MiG can build a track and DESIGNATE it
# (pilot/FBPilot::BfmDesignate, over the bus — the RAD mode does not auto-lock, that is this aircraft's
# own constraint, module.md gap 4h). With a lock the phase flies pursuit instead of the cold search
# that departs it at a merge, and the run measures whether the law holds the airframe while it does.
#
# READING RULE: the run ends at its TIMEOUT, exit 3, BY DESIGN — a fight has no waypoint to arrive at
# (see bfm-basic's head for the full argument). The verdict is read from the telemetry, NOT the exit:
#   - fulcrum must NOT be KO'd by core/FBFlightMonitor at any point (no LOC line in events.log) — that
#     is the departure claim of D1 closed;
#   - bfm_lock_s at the LAST row must be > 0 — the MiG acquired, designated and HELD the lock on its own
#     radar. Measured: 296.3 s of 300, and robust (291.8-296.3 across +-3 m of spawn perturbation);
#   - bfm_pursuit must be a PURSUIT and not `search` for essentially the whole run — measured 296.3 s;
#   - the gun/track channels (bfm_pursuit, gun events) show it is FLYING the fight, not surviving it.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE NO LONGER CLAIMS, and why. bfm_ctrl_s used to be part of the rule above (88.2 s, closing
# to 1.19 nm). Since the roll EXTENT bound (doc/pilot.md 5.7.3) it is 0.0 and the closest approach is
# 1.70 nm — outside the 0.5-1.5 nm control band. That is CAUSAL, not chaos (0.0 in all seven samples of a
# +-3 m spawn perturbation), and it is the declared cost of the bound on THIS airframe: its commanded
# roll-rate cap hook is already 60 deg/s (doc/pilot.md 5.10, screw 4), and the bound makes a SUSTAINED
# roll half the peak, so this jet converts at 30 deg/s and the long one-direction pursuit roll no longer
# arrives. The obvious trade was measured and REJECTED: putting the hook back on the derived 90 deg/s
# restores this file (ctrl_s 86.2, 1.34 nm) and costs a MiG DEPARTURE in duel-merge at t=103.6
# (stall/mush), i.e. it reopens exactly the D1 claim screw 4 closed. A lost control position is a fight
# that does not convert; a departure is a K.O. The hook stays at 60.
#
# GEOMETRY AT T=0: fulcrum sits 2 nm dead astern of bandit, co-altitude at 5,000 m, nose on, at its
# measured corner speed (420 KCAS, `make test-mig29`). bandit runs straight east at 300 KCAS — a
# defender that does not turn, so every degree fulcrum gains is the pursuit law's, and the acquisition
# is the easy one.

unit fulcrum
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 46.67485 6.85148 5000 90.0 420        # 2 nm in trail, co-altitude, this jet's corner speed
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode rad                           # the only pattern wide enough to hold a manoeuvring jet
  set n019_range_nm 10                         # the close-in gate; the fight is inside 2 nm
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r73                             # helmet-cued IR round, the merge weapon
  set store 4 r73
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm                                # FBPilot's fight phase instead of a waypoint route

unit bandit
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.67485 6.90000 5000 90.0 300        # 2 nm ahead, straight and level, does not turn
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off                            # the defender is a target, it does not look
  set datalink off
  wp 46.67485 8.40000 5000 300                # straight east: a stable, non-manoeuvring track to hold
